Z||000000||turbo86se||03-14-2000||10:29 AM||||<BR>The past few days I've been in Frederick, MD, I've seen four Fieros. Oddly enough, they are all GT's! Two black 85GT's, and two red 86 or 87 GT's! I've been to nearly every junkyard in Frederick, and they were all, of course, 84's. One was real nice! Except for the seats and carpet, the interior was mint! I took the instrument cluster (40K miles), and the mint consol-radio-HVAC support NO CRACKS!!!! That's one, I still need to find several more for some Fellow Fiero owners! I cut the living heck out of my hand doing so, oh well.... that's what you get for not wearing gloves!||||reg||10
Z||000001||Shaun41178||03-14-2000||04:41 PM||||Don't forget about Mike Lecompte's white 86 GT with nitrous.  I don't know if you saw his or not but it is a nice ride.  He just had his heads ported and mucho money in them.  He should run 13's with his setup once it is all back togethor.  But you already knew some of that I bet as he told me you went to his house.<P>Shaun||||reg||1
