Z||000003||turbo86se||03-15-2000||12:39 AM||||Yeah Shaun I met Mike Lecompte, pretty cool guy! Showed me a pic of his GT and it was sweet! If I only had a white GT...<BR>Mighty big nitrous bottle! I hope everything turns out alright! <P>Counted two more V6 Fieros! A burgandy 87GT in Frederick and a black 86 or 87SE near Gettysburg on 15. The SE had the Holley scoop but no spoiler. Good thing that gash under my hand didn't affect my golf swing!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||turbo86se||03-16-2000||12:11 PM||||What is going on? Every Fiero I've seen up here is a V6! I got toasted by a nice white GT yesterday afternoon (my 2000 Altima can't quite keep up). I thought I found the first coupe! It's sitting in a repair lot, with "$500 down" on the windshield. Truthfully I don't know what it is. I'll have to get the VIN. It's a red coupe, pointed nose, rear brake light. Wimpy tires, dual exhaust, V6 gauges, and mint interior! I'm thinking 85SE, but no SE sail panels and it has a third brake light. Decklid says Fiero 2m4. No power options, I couldn't open the decklid.  Any ideas?<BR>||||reg||1
